FLOW: setup.qa.flow
DESCRIPTION: From nothing to a working Sylvester in the Grok Bot app — subscription, app, Bot, self-install, updates
LAST UPDATED: 2026-10-20

NOTE: The human only ever talks to Sylvester in the Grok Bot app (desktop: x.ai/bot; phone: "Grok Bot"
in the App Store / Google Play). Everything else happens on the Bot's own cloud computer: the repo is
cloned to /workspace/sylvester-chatwell, household files live in /workspace/sylvester-household, the
nemlig login in /workspace/.sylvester. /workspace survives computer updates; installed packages may not,
which is why every task starts with bin/doctor and falls back to ./install.sh.

================================================================================
SECTION 1: GETTING GROK BOT
================================================================================

TEST: "Buy Premium and sign in to the Grok Bot app"

PRECONDITIONS:
- No Grok subscription yet
- An account at x.ai with Privacy Mode (not "Privacy Mode (Legacy)") — Legacy blocks Grok Bot

STEP 1: "Buy Premium"
GIVEN I open x.ai/pricing
WHEN I buy Grok Premium
THEN my account shows the Premium plan

STEP 2: "Install and sign in"
WHEN I download the Grok Bot app from x.ai/bot (or the App Store / Google Play) and sign in
THEN the app sets up the Bot's computer in the background
AND I land on "Meet a future teammate"

RESULT: I have the Grok Bot app open with an eligible plan.

================================================================================
SECTION 2: CREATING SYLVESTER
================================================================================

TEST: "Create the Bot and point it at the repo — happy path"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Signed in to the Grok Bot app with Premium

STEP 1: "Create the Bot"
WHEN I choose "Create your own" and name the Bot "Sylvester"
THEN an empty chat with Sylvester opens

STEP 2: "Point it at the repo"
WHEN I send "Set yourself up from https://github.com/OneManMobile/sylvester-chatwell — follow BOT.md"
THEN Sylvester tells me in a short message that he is installing
AND within a few minutes he confirms that install and the health check passed
AND the skills onboarding, nemlig-household, recipe-cards, family-week, telegram and sylvester-chatwell
  exist in the Bot's skill library
AND he writes to me in Danish (or my language) as Sylvester Chatwell 🎩

STEP 3: "Next step offered"
THEN he asks for my nemlig.com e-mail to connect nemlig (connect-nemlig.qa.flow)
AND if I'd rather skip, he moves on to the preferences interview (household-preferences.qa.flow)

RESULT: Sylvester is installed on his computer and starts onboarding without me touching a terminal.

================================================================================

TEST: "Setup fails"

PRECONDITIONS:
- The Bot's computer cannot finish ./install.sh (e.g. no network)

STEP 1: "Install fails twice"
WHEN install or doctor fails twice
THEN Sylvester tells me the last error line in one message and stops
AND he does not claim to be set up

RESULT: A broken install is reported plainly, never hidden.

================================================================================
SECTION 3: KEEPING IT WORKING
================================================================================

TEST: "Computer was updated or recreated"

PRECONDITIONS:
- Sylvester was set up before
- Grok Bot updated or recreated the computer (packages gone, /workspace kept)

STEP 1: "Ask for something that needs the tools"
WHEN I ask for a meal plan
THEN Sylvester runs bin/doctor, sees it fail, runs ./install.sh, and continues with my request
AND my preferences, meal log and nemlig login are still there

RESULT: Recovery is automatic; household data survives.

================================================================================

TEST: "Update to the newest version"

STEP 1: "Ask for an update"
WHEN I write "opdater dig" / "update yourself"
THEN Sylvester pulls the repo, re-runs install and doctor, re-saves every skill from the current files
AND tells me it's done
AND my household files and nemlig login are unchanged

RESULT: Updates never wipe the household.
